# The ROAD: flat cobblestones for one 2 m grid cell (x and z from -1 to 1, y = 0 the ground). Written by hand.
# A road is 1.2 m wide. Three objects, used by cableConveyor.pre:
#   RoadHub  - the centre patch (x, z in -0.6 .. 0.6): four stones in a pinwheel around a small one.
#   RoadArmX - the strip from the patch to the cell edge on the +X or -X side: two stones, 0.34 long, CENTRED on the
#              origin (the prefab moves it to x = +-0.83). Mirror-symmetric, so an import that flips an axis keeps it.
#   RoadArmZ - the same strip for the +Z / -Z side.
# Every stone is a low block, 0.05 high, with a 45 degree bevel 0.05 wide: 4 corners on the ground, 4 on its top.
# A strip ends exactly on the cell edge, so two neighbour cells' strips meet there in one bevelled joint.
vt 0 0
vt 1 0
vt 1 1
vt 0 1
vn 0 1 0
vn 0 0.7071 -0.7071
vn 0.7071 0.7071 0
vn 0 0.7071 0.7071
vn -0.7071 0.7071 0
o RoadHub
# stone 1 (1..8)
v -0.60 0 -0.60
v 0.08 0 -0.60
v 0.08 0 -0.14
v -0.60 0 -0.14
v -0.55 0.05 -0.55
v 0.03 0.05 -0.55
v 0.03 0.05 -0.19
v -0.55 0.05 -0.19
